<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσκοπος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκοπέω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>inconsiderate, heedless,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.157
			</span></i>, Timo <i><span class="en">
				5
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄμμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Parm.
					1.35
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσκοποί τινος</span>
			<i>unregardful of</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				462
			</span></i> (lyr.). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-πως</span>”
				<i>heedlessly,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Babr.
					95.39
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>not to be seen, invisible,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάκες ἄ.,</span> of the nether world,
				<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1682
			</span></i> (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hyps.Fr.</u>
				57.21
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>not to be understood, unintelligible,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					816
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
			</span></i>IIII (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρᾶγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. χρόνος</span>
			<i>unknown</i> time, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Tr.</u>
				246
			</span></i>; <i>unimaginable,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. ἁ λώβα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>El.</u>
					864
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); <i>bewildering, strange,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἤργασαι δέ μ᾽ ἄσκοπα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1315
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄσκεπτος</span>
			, <i>unconsidered,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				7.432
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
